{
  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "The current best (config_025: pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted, acc=0.635) has established that multiprofile + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted is a strong architecture, but the RNA encoder remains at the simple PCA baseline (pca_n2000). No experiment has yet tested a learned RNA encoder (scvi_n200) in this best-known regime. This is the largest unexplored design dimension: whether a generative, learned encoder can capture richer transcriptomic structure than 2000-dim PCA and push accuracy beyond 0.635. Config_037 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) isolates this single variable against the current champion, making the result directly interpretable. Under a limited budget, resolving whether the RNA encoder is a bottleneck (or whether PCA is already near-saturating) is more informative than testing the small weighted-vs-concat interaction (Δ≈0.006) or the already-penalized transformer aggregation."
}

